Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• ORDERS."order_id": primary key, join to ORDER_ITEMS."order_id".  
• ORDERS."created_at": order‑creation timestamp (micro‑seconds since epoch) – filter on 2019‑06‑01 → 2019‑12‑31 and derive calendar month.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."order_id": joins to ORDERS to inherit the order date.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."product_id": joins to PRODUCTS."id" to obtain category & cost.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": item‑level revenue.  
• PRODUCTS."id": join key.  
• PRODUCTS."category": product category used in the monthly breakdown.  
• PRODUCTS."cost": unit cost; profit = sale_price – cost.  

(Other columns such as status, gender, etc. are not required for the requested report but are left available if future slicing is needed.)

Typical conditions that might be useful  
• ORDERS."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836799000000   -- (2019‑06‑01 .. 2019‑12‑31, micro‑seconds)  
• PRODUCT."category" IS NOT NULL  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (each different, all limited to 20 rows, all column names enclosed in double quotes).  
Adjust the numeric boundaries if you find the micro‑second values differ slightly when you inspect the data.

```sql
-- 1) Quick glance at raw order headers for 2019
SELECT "order_id",
       "status",
       "created_at"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836799000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) See the earliest and latest order timestamps present in the whole table
SELECT MIN("created_at") AS "min_created_at",
       MAX("created_at") AS "max_created_at"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS";
```

```sql
-- 3) Distinct year‑month values actually present in 2019 (micro‑seconds truncated to month using integer math)
SELECT DISTINCT TO_CHAR( DATE_FROM_PARTS(1970,1,1) 
                         + ("created_at"/1000000)::BIGINT * INTERVAL '1 SECOND', 'YYYY-MM') AS "yyyy_mm"
FROM "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"
WHERE "created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836799000000
ORDER BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Look at order items joined to their parent orders for June 2019
SELECT oi."order_id",
       oi."product_id",
       oi."sale_price",
       o."created_at"           AS "order_created_at"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"       o
       ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
WHERE  o."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1561939199000000   -- June 2019
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Which product categories were sold in 2019?
SELECT DISTINCT p."category"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     p
       ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Sample revenue & cost side by side for a few line items in July 2019
SELECT oi."order_id",
       oi."product_id",
       p."category",
       oi."sale_price",
       p."cost"                            AS "unit_cost",
       (oi."sale_price" - p."cost")        AS "profit"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"       o  ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     p  ON p."id"      = oi."product_id"
WHERE  o."created_at" BETWEEN 1561939200000000 AND 1564617599000000   -- July 2019
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Aggregate: month‑by‑category revenue for June 2019
SELECT TO_CHAR( DATE_FROM_PARTS(1970,1,1) + (o."created_at"/1000000)::BIGINT*INTERVAL '1 SECOND', 'YYYY-MM') AS "yyyymm",
       p."category",
       COUNT(DISTINCT o."order_id")        AS "orders_cnt",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                AS "revenue"
FROM   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDER_ITEMS"  oi
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."ORDERS"       o  ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
JOIN   "THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."THELOOK_ECOMMERCE"."PRODUCTS"     p  ON p."id"      = oi."product_id"
WHERE  o."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1561939199000000   -- June 2019
GROUP  BY 1,2
ORDER  BY 1,2
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
