Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• ORDERS."order_id": primary key, join to ORDER_ITEMS."order_id".  
• ORDERS."created_at": order‑creation timestamp (micro‑seconds since epoch) – filter on 2019‑06‑01 → 2019‑12‑31 and derive calendar month.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."order_id": joins to ORDERS to inherit the order date.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."product_id": joins to PRODUCTS."id" to obtain category & cost.  
• ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": item‑level revenue.  
• PRODUCTS."id": join key.  
• PRODUCTS."category": product category used in the monthly breakdown.  
• PRODUCTS."cost": unit cost; profit = sale_price – cost.  

(Other columns such as status, gender, etc. are not required for the requested report but are left available if future slicing is needed.)

Typical conditions that might be useful  
• ORDERS."created_at" BETWEEN 1559347200000000 AND 1577836799000000   -- (2019‑06‑01 .. 2019‑12‑31, micro‑seconds)  
• PRODUCT."category" IS NOT NULL  

